# Security & Secrets — CRITICAL

## Never Commit to Git

- OpenShift credentials (username/password, kubeadmin tokens)
- SealedSecrets **private** keys (only the public cert may be committed)
- Any `*.kubeconfig` or `kubeconfig` files
- Ansible vault passwords or plain-text vault files
- Any file matching patterns in `.gitignore`

## Credential Handling Pattern

- Cluster API URL, username, and password → passed at runtime via env vars or Ansible extra-vars
- Secrets that must live in the repo → encrypt with `ansible-vault` (encrypted blobs only)
- SealedSecrets private key → shared with `devops-ai-agentic`, stored in `ansible/inventory/group_vars/all/vault.yml` (encrypted)
- Application secrets (GitHub token, backend secret, etc.) → committed as `SealedSecret` CRs

## Sealing a New Secret

```bash
# Fetch the public cert from the running cluster
kubeseal --fetch-cert \
  --controller-name=sealed-secrets-controller \
  --controller-namespace=sealed-secrets \
  > /tmp/sealed-secrets.crt

# Seal a secret
kubectl create secret generic my-secret \
  --from-literal=key=value \
  --dry-run=client -o yaml | \
  kubeseal --cert /tmp/sealed-secrets.crt \
  --format yaml > k8s/developer-hub/instance/my-secret-sealed.yaml
```
